=== Compound dome ===
Also called ''domes on pendentives''{{sfn|Karydis|2012|pp=362–363}} or ''pendentive domes''{{sfn|Hassan|Mazloomi|Omer|2010|p=105}} (a term also applied to sail vaults), compound domes have pendentives that support a smaller diameter dome immediately above them, as in the Hagia Sophia, or a drum and dome, as in many Renaissance and post-Renaissance domes, with both forms resulting in greater height.{{sfn|Catholic}}

